    "jeff-ingest-1761200000": {
      "ingest": {
        "aim": [
          {
            "kind": "vision",
            "text": "fm-proxy lets any ordinary OpenAI Chat Completions client use Apple's on-device Foundation Model (fm serve, model 'system') on macOS 27 without code changes, by correcting fm serve's deviations from the OpenAI spec on a loopback-only proxy, for local research only (licence conflict acknowledged)."
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, I can get a single JSON chat completion with accurate token usage from the on-device model, in order to use Apple's model without code changes. [api: POST /v1/chat/completions non-stream]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, I can stream a chat completion as SSE ending in exactly one finish_reason and real usage, in order to render output incrementally and account for tokens. [api: POST /v1/chat/completions stream]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, I can force a tool call (tool_choice required or named) and receive real tool_calls, streaming or not, in order to drive function calling despite fm serve's broken tool parser. [api: forced dispatch]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, I can send structured-output schemas generated by pydantic/zod/TypeBox ($defs/$ref, nullable type arrays) and get constrained JSON, in order to use structured output unmodified. [api: response_format]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, I can send tools with rich nested schemas and optional descriptions without the whole request 400ing, in order to reuse my existing tool definitions. [api: tools]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, I receive typed OpenAI-shaped errors (content_filter, context_length_exceeded, rate_limit_exceeded, invalid_request_error, cyclic_schema, upstream_unreachable) and transient failures are retried invisibly, in order to branch on cause instead of parsing Apple prose. [api: errors]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, my max_tokens, stop and developer-role fields are honoured, in order that standard request parameters behave per the OpenAI spec. [api: param fixups]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an operator, my fm serve is protected from a cyclic $defs schema that would hang it permanently, in order to keep the server alive. [api: cyclic guard]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As a browser-based client, I can call the proxy cross-origin, in order to use the model from a web page. [api: CORS, header scrubbing]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an OpenAI-SDK client, I can list models and check health, in order to discover the 'system' model and liveness. [api: GET /v1/models, /health]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As a client consuming content, I can opt in to stripping leaked chat-template markers, in order to get clean text while audits can still see the upstream bug by default. [env: FM_STRIP_TEMPLATE_MARKERS]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As an operator, I can start and stop fm serve plus the proxy with one command and configure ports, binary and retries, in order to run the stack without orphaned processes. [cli: fm-launch.sh, env]"
          },
          {
            "kind": "story",
            "text": "As a maintainer, I can verify the proxy against a live fm serve, record a deterministic wire baseline, run unit/integration tests, and regenerate the fm CLI reference per build, in order to audit each macOS build and refactor safely. [cli: deviation-probe, wire-baseline, node --test, gen-fm-docs]"
          }
        ],
        "entrypoints": [
          "POST /v1/chat/completions (non-streaming)",
          "POST /v1/chat/completions (streaming)",
          "POST /v1/chat/completions (forced tool_choice dispatch)",
          "GET /v1/models",
          "GET /health",
          "OPTIONS * (CORS preflight)",
          "cli:fm-launch.sh [--fm-port --proxy-port --fm-bin --health-timeout]",
          "cli:node fm-proxy.js (env PROXY_PORT FM_PORT FM_BIN FM_STRIP_TEMPLATE_MARKERS CORS_ORIGIN FM_MAX_RETRIES FM_RETRY_BASE_MS FM_RETRY_CAP_MS)",
          "cli:node tools/deviation-probe.js [port]",
          "cli:node tools/wire-baseline.js <out.json>",
          "cli:python3 tools/gen-fm-docs.py [--fm --outdir]",
          "cli:node --test"
        ],
        "entrypoints_reported": [
          "POST /v1/chat/completions (non-streaming)",
          "POST /v1/chat/completions (streaming)",
          "POST /v1/chat/completions (forced tool_choice dispatch)",
          "GET /v1/models",
          "GET /health",
          "OPTIONS * (CORS preflight)",
          "cli:fm-launch.sh [--fm-port --proxy-port --fm-bin --health-timeout]",
          "cli:node fm-proxy.js (env PROXY_PORT FM_PORT FM_BIN FM_STRIP_TEMPLATE_MARKERS CORS_ORIGIN FM_MAX_RETRIES FM_RETRY_BASE_MS FM_RETRY_CAP_MS)",
          "cli:node tools/deviation-probe.js [port]",
          "cli:node tools/wire-baseline.js <out.json>",
          "cli:python3 tools/gen-fm-docs.py [--fm --outdir]",
          "cli:node --test"
        ],
